            <ArticleTitle>[Habitat and incidence of respiratory organs diseases in the Samara population].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There was performed the assessment of habitat quality for Samara population. Risk factors for prevalence of respiratory diseases (pneumonia, allergic rhinitis, asthma) in children, teenagers and adults were revealed to be formaldehyde, phenol, hydrogen sulfide in the ambient, cadmium and copper in the soil.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
